Title: Ai's Teachings
Order: 16
Production Code: 1x16

INT. TELASSAR - AI'S CHAMBER - NIGHT

AMB: quiet, a single lamp

Late into the night, [[Ai]] questions [[Reuel Briggs]] about the world he's left behind.

AI
Is it true that the Ethiopian is counted less than other men, where you come from?

REUEL BRIGGS
(a flush of shame)
It is true, Ai. And I played the coward's part in hiding from it rather than fighting it.

AI
And yet from Ethiopia came every art your modern world calls its own.

Ai describes Telassar's government — a virgin queen named Candace, chosen anew from among the city's daughters every fifteen years, ruling until the royal line itself returns.

EXT. MOUNTAIN GORGE - DAY (LATER)

AMB: a narrow rocky pass, rushing water

Reuel travels with Ai's party toward the inner city. A lion blocks the only path forward. Reuel steps to the front of the column and fixes it with a level, unbroken stare.

SFX: a low growl, receding

The lion backs away, defeated by nothing but his gaze. His companions murmur in awe.

TELASSAR ATTENDANT
Truly, he is the King.

INT. TELASSAR - INNER CITY - PRESENCE CHAMBER - CONTINUOUS

AMB: distant lyres, a hushed court

They reach the inner city's presence chamber, where [[Queen Candace]] receives them, and prostrates herself before Reuel the moment she sees him.

QUEEN CANDACE
O Ergamenes — hast thou indeed returned to thine inheritance?

Her resemblance to Dianthe is close enough to bring him to the edge of tears.

QUEEN CANDACE (CONT'D)
And dost thou agree, and art thou willing, my lord?

REUEL BRIGGS
(moved, uncertain)
Queen Candace, thy beauty dazzles me. I will fulfill my destiny, and cleave to thee until the end.

She takes a ring of dull gold, its stone cut to a lotus lily, and places it on his hand herself.

QUEEN CANDACE
Thus do I claim thee for all eternity.
